      "id": "7ukxerq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "4.1.1 Governor"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yk4uedj",
      "content": "The Governor is the constitutional head of the state, appointed by the President of India. The Governor acts as the nominal head of the executive. The Council of Ministers is headed by the Chief Minister and is responsible to the State Legislative Assembly."
    },
    {
      "id": "hsh35aw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "4.1.2 State Legislature"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hsy5a90",
      "content": "Gujarat has a unicameral legislature — the Gujarat Legislative Assembly (Vidhan Sabha). It has 182 seats. The Governor is the constitutional head; the Chief Minister is the head of the government."
    },
    {
      "id": "ny0xkws",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Total Seats in Vidhan Sabha: 182",
        "SC Reserved Seats: 13",
        "ST Reserved Seats: 27",
        "Sessions: Budget (February), Monsoon (July–August), Winter (December)"
      ]
    },
